WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.180
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and some new
pics of Ben Affleck’s Batmobile just dropped.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.520
They were taken by a random kid on instagram.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.880
He even took on with himself sitting in the
cockpit.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.879
So let’s take a look and see what we all
think.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:20.030
If you are finding me for the first time.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.490
I’m doing DC movie and tv videos every week.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.750
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:30.190
Here’s what the pictures show, it’s has
some of the Christopher Nolan Tumbler DNA

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:36.530
in it, but it looks a lot more like the Batmobile
from the Arkham Knight game.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.892
Slightly less fortified but much more aggressive
and agile looking than the christopher nolan

00:00:40.892 --> 00:00:41.892
version.

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:46.329
The story of the movie supposedly takes a
lot from Frank Miller’s Dark Knight Returns,

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:50.280
so not going with the old school Bat-Tank
is a big departure.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.050
This feels much more modern.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.890
The culture today is just shrinking cars down.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.350
Frank Miller’s version was designed for
all out open war.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.390
This one feels more like a knife.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.670
One of the big problems with the Tumbler was
it had a hard time with corners just because

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.369
of those massive tires.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:14.509
Does anyone remember the Michael Keaton batmobile
from Batman Returns?

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:18.280
And how it used the grappling hook to swing
around tight corners.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.170
Physics, we don’t need no stinkin’ physics.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:28.180
I am of the opinion that this batmobile, thus
far looks the closest to something you might

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.070
actually see driving around today.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.350
Unless you count Adam West’s batmobile.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.450
Which was also a slightly modified car.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:45.109
Not a slightly modified assault tank.

00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:49.320
Just for fun let’s look at all the most
popular Batmobiles.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.979
If you include all the comics, movies, tv
shows and video games.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:56.840
There have been almost 300 different variations
on the car.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.450
But that number includes a lot of minor changes.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.520
So here’s all the major versions:

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.369
There was the first one, it was a Red Sedan
and was just called “his car”.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:08.429
There wasn’t anything special about it.

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:10.300
It debuted in Detective Comics #27.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.700
The started calling it the Batmobile in Issue
#48.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:21.750
In Issue #30 they upgraded the engine, but
it wasn’t until Batman #5 in 1941 that they

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:28.660
made the body much sleeker, darkened the color
and added a Bat hood ornament and a fin.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.190
Three pages after it debuted.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.020
The joker forced it off a cliff.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.600
But the same design of car returned in the
next issue.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.300
I think there was a joke in the Tim Burton
Batman about Bruce Wayne having more cars

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.000
than he knew what to do with.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Then in 1944 the Batmobile was featured on
the cover of a comic for the first time in

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.300
Batman #20.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.980
This design was so popular it became the default
Batmobile for the rest of the 1940s.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:03:01.480
Then of course was the 1965 Adam West version.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.790
It was made by George Barris from a Ford Futura,
which was a failed concept car that they never

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.260
put into production.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:13.530
He modified it to give it the look and interior
functions.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:21.030
In 1973 the Superfriends cartoon introduced
a modified version of the Adam West car.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.810
They just straightened the lines, changed
the hood and added the batman decals on the

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.810
doors.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:30.820
This was the first car to feature the yellow
batman symbol on the car.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:35.050
Frank Miller introduced a full on assault
tank in his 1985 Dark Knight Returns book.

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:38.320
In terms of size, it is the largest batmobile
ever.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.430
It takes up three car lanes.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:45.860
The joke he makes in the story is that only
something “not from this planet can damage

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.860
it”.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.230
Of course talking about Superman.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:55.090
Then in 1989 came the Tim Burton design which
lasted through both of his films.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.361
The body was a complete custom fab built on
a chevy V8.

00:03:58.361 --> 00:04:05.370
The added major things like the jet turbine
but kept some of the 1930s design with the

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.640
tail fins.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:12.930
They modified the Tim Burton design slightly
for Batman the Animated Series.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:17.120
Thanks to animation being able to fudge the
laws of physics they were able to combine

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:23.540
a lot of different elements from previous
batmobiles to the concept.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.150
Then in 1995 for Batman Forever they modified
the Tim Burton design to make it look like

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:33.750
it actually had ribs, added lighting highlights,
a much smaller cockpit more gadgetry inside

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.220
and a much larger fin.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.061
This was the beginning of the Joel Schumacher
era.

00:04:37.061 --> 00:04:42.490
In Batman and Robin a couple years later then
pushed the cockpit way back and accentuated

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.530
the grill.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:51.910
Supposedly they said they wanted the car to
have a larger than life presence when it was

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:52.910
on screen.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:05:01.490
Almost every panel inside and outside of the
car lit up.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:06.300
In 1995 when they started the New Animated
series they completely re-did the car to make

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.060
it much simpler.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:14.960
That series only ran till 1999, but the design
of this car was also used in the comics.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:27.070
Then in 2005, eight years after Batman and
Robin Christopher nolan introduced the Tumbler.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:30.120
A modified army vehicle made to jump canyons
and lay temporary bridges.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.960
Throughout Nolan’s Dark Knight Trilogy they
made modifications to the design like giving

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:48.940
it remote control features and 

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.910
the Batpod Motorcycle.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:56.730
The first Arkham Asylum video game in 2009
introduced a slightly modified Tim Burton

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:02.300
batmobile.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:07.140
The most recent revision, not counting Zack
Snyder’s batmobile is the Arkham Knight

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.140
Game.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.420
This game isn’t going to be released till
2015 but as you can see, the design combines

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:17.860
a lot of the urban maneuvering features with
the assault weaponry of the tank.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:21.530
Right now I still really love the Tumbler,
but my favorite Batmobile is probably going

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:24.870
to be the Arkham Knight one from next year.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.070
My favorite animated one is from the Batman
the Animated Series.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.700
Now it’s your turn, let me know, which version
of the batmobile is your favorite?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:37.670
Like I said, there have been almost 300 different
versions, but when you’re a billionaire

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.330
it’s no big deal.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.200
On a related note, don’t you think it’s
interesting that Stephen Amell doesn’t have

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.920
a Green Arrow car on Arrow.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.820
I’m glad, I don’t think it would work
with the tone of the show and the look they’re

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.820
